vkd3d-proton: programmable sample positions on VK_EXT_sample_locations

ProgrammableSamplePositionsTier was hard-wired to 0 and SetSamplePositions
was a stub.  Below tier 1 the Windows D3D12 runtime refuses
ResolveSubresourceRegion outright ("Device does not support programmable
MSAA, and therefore does not support ResolveSubresourceRegion()"): the
list's Close fails, the device is removed, and sampler feedback maps -- only
readable through DECODE/ENCODE_SAMPLER_FEEDBACK resolves -- are unusable,
which is what stopped 3DMark's Sampler Feedback test at Present.

  - device: enable VK_EXT_sample_locations and report tier 1 when its
    locations change between draws of a render pass
    (variableSampleLocations), cover D3D12's 1/16-pixel steps over [-8, 7]
    (4 sub-pixel bits, [0, 15/16]) and every multisampled count the device
    renders; tier 2 also needs a 2x2 pixel grid at every count.  Graphics
    pipeline libraries build the multisample state in a separate fragment
    output library that does not carry the locations, so tier 0 there.
    MoltenVK on Apple GPUs (Metal setSamplePositions per render pass, 2x/4x,
    1x1 grid, MoltenVK restarts the Metal pass when they change) is tier 1.
  - pipelines: multisampled pipelines whose rasterization count takes
    locations get VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_SAMPLE_LOCATIONS_EXT with
    sampleLocationsEnable.  The location count must equal the rasterization
    count, so these pipelines keep a static count (no dynamic rasterization
    samples) and a target of another count takes the sample count variant
    (render target changes reselect the pipeline unless it is dynamic).
  - command list: SetSamplePositions is list state (reset with the list,
    (0, 0) restores the standard pattern); before a draw the list emits the
    programmed pattern, or the D3D12 standard pattern -- also Vulkan's
    standard locations -- when none is set or it was set for another sample
    count, and re-emits when the bound pipeline's count changes.  D3D12
    position (X, Y) maps to ((X + 8) / 16, (Y + 8) / 16).  A 2x2 pattern on
    a tier 1 device keeps the first pixel's positions.  One sample per pixel
    has no Vulkan locations (MoltenVK takes 2x/4x); a single programmed
    position is the pixel centre moved by (X, Y) / 16, which equals
    rasterizing everything moved the opposite way, so the list shifts its
    viewports by -(X, Y) / 16 while a 1-sample pattern and a 1-sample draw
    are current (coverage and interpolation follow; SV_Position of a
    sample-frequency shader keeps the pixel centre).
  - resources: multisampled depth/stencil images are created
    SAMPLE_LOCATIONS_COMPATIBLE_DEPTH.  Layout transitions do not pass
    VkSampleLocationsInfoEXT: depth rendered with programmed positions is
    only guaranteed through transitions on drivers without depth layout
    work (MoltenVK, the only driver behind AnyOS's guest D3D12).

HLSL GetSamplePosition / GetRenderTargetSamplePosition keep dxil-spirv's
standard-pattern table.

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/command.c b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
index 76f884d..3a7bfd2 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/command.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
@@ -8541,6 +8541,96 @@ static bool d3d12_command_list_update_raygen_state(struct d3d12_command_list *li
